 "kind": "recipe",
 "metadata": {
  "alignment": "standard",
  "description": "DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (deepseek-ai, MIT; native MXFP4 experts, FP8 dense weights, DSpark speculative decoding, tool calling and vision) on three DGX Sparks with SGLang tensor parallel 3 over the ConnectX-7 fabric. Basis: MiaAI-Lab's three-Spark kit (AGPL-3.0-or-later, boot.py, the Engram row-store and decode adapters vendored unchanged, on the lmsysorg/sglang dev-dsv41 image), with upstream's EP 1, 256k default context, 750k-token KV pin and four-request concurrency. Rank 2's attention shard is zero padding (heads 64 to 96). The two Engram tables (189 GiB) are read from the checkpoint by an NVMe row store; upstream's optional per-node repacking (./start.sh pack) is not part of the recipe, so upstream's throughput figures (51 tok/s prose at one stream, about 2,000 tok/s prefill) are its own claims on the packed layout, not measured here. Memory is very tight (about 6 GB left on the head); Vonk physical three-Spark acceptance is pending.",
  "tags": [
   "candidate",
   "chat",
   "deepseek-v4.1",
   "distributed",
   "dspark",
   "engram",
   "multimodal",
   "mxfp4",
   "reasoning",
   "sglang",
   "spark",
   "speculative-decoding",
   "tool-use"
  ],
  "title": "DeepSeek V4.1 Flash SGLang three Sparks (Mia)"
 },
